      <h2>Home-labbing</h2>
      <p>Fifteen years of a homelab, told in photos: four homes since 2011, and two matching 30U racks along the way. One still runs the lab; the other now holds the batteries for the <a href='/powerwall.html'>powerwall</a>. Every photo is in the <a href='/gallery/liskl-networks-datacenter.html'>datacenter gallery</a>, and the current setup is <a href='#today'>at the bottom</a>.</p>

      <h2 id='georgia'>Georgia <small>2011 &ndash; 2014</small></h2>
      <p>The lab started in Georgia: one enclosed rack, a KVM drawer and <em>prometheus</em>, the VMware vSphere box, followed by OpenStack across a set of Dell servers. By 2014 it was also running USB bitcoin miners, just before the move to Florida.</p>
