      <h2 id='software'>The software</h2>
      <p>Four homes, three platforms. <em>prometheus</em> ran VMware vSphere, and OpenStack followed across the Dell servers, both while the lab was still in Georgia.
        Kubernetes took over in 2015, starting at 1.0, and still runs the lab today. The cluster has since moved onto the mini rack, and the big rack now only keeps storage online.</p>

      <h2 id='today'>What it runs on today</h2>
      <ul class='sub'>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Edge</strong> - OPNsense on a Deciso DEC2700, with two internet uplinks (fiber and satellite)</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Compute</strong> - a three-node k3s cluster (vulcan, worker-02, worker-03) on Minisforum BD795i SE Mini-ITX boards: Ryzen 9 7945HX (16 cores, 32 threads), 128&nbsp;GB of DDR5 (the spec sheet says 96) and a 2&nbsp;TB NVMe each</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Out-of-band</strong> - a JetKVM per node, mounted in the 10-inch rack above them</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Network</strong> - an all-fiber 10&nbsp;Gb SFP+ fabric; each node bonds two Intel 82599 ports into 20&nbsp;Gb. Ubiquiti EdgeSwitches and UniFi cover the rest of the house</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Storage</strong> - gringotts, a Dell PowerEdge R730xd running TrueNAS SCALE, serving iSCSI and NFS to the cluster</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Delivery</strong> - Flux GitOps; this site is built into an image and served from the cluster</li>
      </ul>
      <p>More photos, in order, in the <a href='/gallery/liskl-networks-datacenter.html'>datacenter gallery</a>.</p>
